@@ -98,7 +98,24 @@ ### Ticket
 
 **Immutability enforcement:** the write-once rule is enforced on the `Ticket` model (`updating` hook), so it applies to Eloquent saves only — mass updates through the query builder (`Ticket::query()->update(...)`) bypass it and must not be used on issued tickets.
 
-**Single-ticket call (scope note):** `Ticket::call()` marks one waiting ticket as `called` (entity-membership checked, exactly-once). This minimal domain primitive proves the mutable `status`/`called_*` fields. Deterministic call-next selection (priority + age + 3-ticket fairness) is implemented by `App\Actions\CallNextTicket` with the three call-panel modes below (`any` applies fairness; `priority_only`/`normal_only` ignore it); AuthZ stays out of scope per #20 and HTTP/Livewire panels remain future work.
+**Single-ticket call (scope note):** `Ticket::call()` marks one waiting ticket as `called` (exactly-once, and only for a caller with call access to the queue, see [Queue Management and Call Access](#queue-management-and-call-access)). This minimal domain primitive proves the mutable `status`/`called_*` fields. Deterministic call-next selection (priority + age + 3-ticket fairness) is implemented by `App\Actions\CallNextTicket` with the three call-panel modes below (`any` applies fairness; `priority_only`/`normal_only` ignore it). Both call paths enforce the same call access; HTTP/Livewire panels remain future work.
+
+### Queue Management and Call Access
+
+Queues are managed by `App\Actions\CreateQueue`, `App\Actions\UpdateQueue` and `App\Actions\SetQueueAccess`. Every decision is made by `App\Policies\QueuePolicy`, and actions authorize before they write anything.
+
+| Operation | Who can | Rules |
+| --------- | ------- | ----- |
+| Create a queue | Owner, admin of the entity | Name trimmed, 1–255 characters. New queues are active. |
+| Rename, change slug, activate or deactivate | Owner, admin of the entity | Any combination in one call; omitted fields are unchanged. |
+| Delete a queue | Nobody | Not supported. A queue is retired by deactivating it. |
+| Grant or revoke queue access | Owner, admin of the entity | Sets the permissions of one membership on one queue. An empty list revokes. |
+| Call tickets on a queue | Owner, admin of the entity; employee with a `call` grant on that queue | Any other user is denied, in every call mode. |
+
+- **Slug:** defaults to the slugified name (`Atendimento Geral` → `atendimento-geral`). An explicit slug is slugified too. A slug is unique within its entity, so the same slug may exist in two entities. Taking another queue's slug is rejected.
+- **Deactivation:** `is_active = false` keeps the queue's tickets. Issuing or calling on an inactive queue fails with `InactiveQueueException`. Reactivation is allowed.
+- **Access grants:** the only permission today is `call`. Grants belong to one membership and one queue. Employees cannot grant access, including to themselves. Owners and admins do not need a grant to call.
+- **Audit:** each grant (`queue.access.granted`) and revoke (`queue.access.revoked`) is written to the `audit` log with the acting user, the queue and the membership. Revoking a membership that has no grant writes nothing.
 
