@@ -148,6 +148,8 @@ ## Modeling Notes
 - **Account vs member:** `users` is the login account (Laravel Auth); `entity_memberships` is the user's link to the entity with role.
 - **User↔entity cardinality:** `entity_memberships` is N:N by design (allows future multi-entity). In MVP, "one user per entity" rule is enforced in application; no global UK on `user_id`.
 - **Owner invariant:** `entities` has no `owner_membership_id` FK. The single-owner constraint lives on `entity_memberships` via `entities.owner_seq` (generated `CASE WHEN role='owner' THEN 1 ELSE NULL END`) and a unique `(entity_id, owner_seq)` index — portable across SQLite + MySQL. Bootstrapping creates the entity then its owner row in one transaction; ownership transfer demotes the old owner to `admin` and promotes the target `admin` to `owner` in the same transaction. The generated column goes NULL during both steps, so the transient no-owner state is allowed (only a 2nd `role='owner'` row for the same entity collides).
+- **Queue access:** `queue_access` (`entity_membership_id`, `queue_id`, `permissions`, timestamps) has cascading foreign keys on both sides and a unique `(entity_membership_id, queue_id)`. Its `permissions` values are `QueuePermission` (`call` is the only one). Grants and revokes go through `App\Actions\SetQueueAccess`, which keeps the membership and queue in the same entity.
+- **Queue slug:** `queues.slug` is unique per entity, not globally. It defaults to the slugified name and is always slugified. Queues are deactivated (`is_active`), never deleted, so their tickets stay reachable.
 - **Numeric priority:** `tickets.priority` is an integer — **higher value, more prioritized**. Named levels (normal/priority/80+) are configurable presets per entity mapping to values; sorting uses the number.
 - **Ticket write-once:** ticket is **single-use** and receives **one single call**. All fields are immutable after issuance, **except** `called_at` and `called_by_user_id`, filled at call time. No call history table.
 - **Ticket ↔ totem:** ticket knows only its **queue** (`queue_id`). `channel` records origin type; no FK to `totems`.
